Body:
Aixy is a concrete gateway use case for this reconciliation.

Aixy exposes an authenticated, project-scoped `GET /v1/models` endpoint. It returns both provider-qualified direct models (for example `openai/gpt-...`) and tenant-defined virtual routing models in the `aixy/<alias>` namespace. The latter can be created or changed by the customer, so they cannot be represented in a global models.dev snapshot.

The models.dev entry is still valuable as a metadata seed and bounded fallback, but runtime availability should come from the authenticated endpoint. Ideally OpenCode would:

- reconcile models.dev metadata with `/models`;
- add IDs returned only by the endpoint, including virtual models;
- hide unavailable catalog entries for the current credential/project;
- preserve explicit config overrides; and
- fall back to the last known/static catalog on timeout or malformed responses.

Aixy already returns the standard OpenAI model-list envelope and can be used to test account-scoped discovery. We would be happy to help validate the behavior, including virtual models whose capability metadata must represent the guarantees of the route rather than a single underlying model.
